From 99b6a2b768904b3f947acbe6810a4607f8c6668f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Scholz <jonathan.scholz@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 26 Apr 2026 04:58:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] tools: add video_analyze_tool (gemini-3-flash via
 openrouter)

Adds a video_analyze tool parallel to vision_analyze so the gateway can
handle inbound WhatsApp/Telegram video attachments instead of looping on
the image-only vision tool.

- video_analyze_tool(video_url, user_prompt, model=None) accepts http(s)
  URLs and absolute local paths. Sends video inline to the configured
  auxiliary vision provider (Gemini 3 Flash Preview via OpenRouter) using
  an image_url content block with a data:video/mp4;base64,... URL.
- For videos > 20MB or when the inline call fails, falls back to ffmpeg
  keyframe extraction (6 evenly-spaced frames, scaled to 1280px) and runs
  vision_analyze on each, concatenating descriptions.
- Registers the tool under the existing 'vision' toolset (and the
  hermes-acp / hermes-api-server bundles) so it's available wherever
  vision_analyze is.
- gateway/run.py: classifies inbound video media and auto-enriches the
  message text via _enrich_message_with_video, mirroring the existing
  vision/transcription enrichment pipelines.
- agent/display.py + context_compressor.py: render video_analyze tool
  calls in the live UI and compressed history.

Live-tested with /tmp/test.mp4 (3s testsrc, 14KB): inline call returned
a coherent description without falling back to keyframes. Keyframe
fallback also verified end-to-end on the same file.
